WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.650
Unlike our favorite comic book characters,
the origin stories of silver screen superheroes

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:10.780
often involve more steamed chicken breasts
and stationary bikes than kryptonite and dead

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.830
parents.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:16.170
But while the actors get paid to look the
part, it's the stunt doubles who take the

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.370
hits, the falls, and the rubber bullets, all
without any of the glory.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:24.741
Let's go behind the scenes to highlight some
of these brave performers who toil in the

00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:28.770
shadows to bring the Earth's mightiest heroes
to life.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.060
Ingrid Kleinig—Harley Quinn

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:36.030
Ingrid Kleinig has been in the biz for a while
and definitely knows the ropes.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:41.219
She's done stunt work on movies as diverse
as Superman Returns, Australia, and Iron Sky,

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:46.149
but Kleinig really broke into the big-time
as Evangeline Lilly's stunt double in The

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.339
Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey.

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:53.269
Still, if she's had one defining part, it's
her work as Margot Robbie's stunt double on

00:00:53.269 --> 00:00:54.629
Suicide Squad.

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:59.670
She and Robbie—who's a dancer herself—became
friends while tag-teaming the stunts for Harley

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:00.670
Quinn.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:05.280
They even held a long-running contest to see
who could hold their breath the longest underwater.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.080
In the end they both topped five minutes.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.250
That's the kind of skill that comes in handy
when your job involves crashing face-first

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.440
through a Lamborghini windshield in a water
tank.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.980
Will Erichson—Deadpool

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:22.880
Over roughly a decade, Will Erichson has built
up a huge Hollywood stunt resume, appearing

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.880
in everything from TRON: Legacy to Wayward
Pines.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:31.270
In 2016, Erichson scored big when he landed
the part of Ryan Reynolds' stunt double during

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.580
the filming of Deadpool.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.860
Along with a team of other stuntmen, Erichson
helped bring our favorite regenerating degenerate

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.200
to the big screen.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.390
In particular, Erichson was instrumental in
the SUV scene at the start of the movie.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:48.130
And for that, Erichson, you have our heartfelt
thanks.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.100
Richard Bradshaw—Wolverine

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.450
Richard Bradshaw's prolific stunt career spans
nearly three decades of work on television

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.010
and the big screen.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:01.810
You've seen his work in movies like The Fifth
Element, Titanic, and Tomorrow Never Dies,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:06.730
and he's also been involved in the production
of Game of Thrones, serving as both a performer

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:11.540
and the show's assistant stunt coordinator
for more than two dozen episodes.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.130
In the X-Men franchise, Bradshaw worked as
a performer and stunt double for Hugh Jackman

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:22.319
in X-Men 2, The Last Stand, X-Men Origins:
Wolverine, and Days of Future Past.

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.420
William Spencer—Spider-Man

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.270
William Spencer earned the nickname "The Skate
Ninja" on YouTube for his unusual skateboarding

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:33.950
style, but he probably never thought his board
would give him a career in the movies.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.070
The Amazing Spider-Man director Marc Webb
had other ideas.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.760
For his first outing with the web-head, Webb
wanted to do something completely different,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.610
and that involved...this:

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.680
"... I don't know which way I'm going…"

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:55.290
Spencer, who'd spent a few years picking up
spare paychecks doing light stunt work on

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:59.490
movies like Jonah Hex and Project X, didn't
even make it to his Spider-Man audition.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:03.970
Ultimately, the filmmakers couldn't find what
they were looking for and looped back around

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:09.270
to Spencer, who ended up as Andrew Garfield's
double for both Amazing Spider-Man movies.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.250
Tony McFarr—Star-Lord

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:16.890
Tony McFarr got started as a stunt performer
in 2011, and since then he's built up an impressive

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:21.030
stunt resume, appearing in dozens of television
series and films.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:26.650
With his role in 2015's Jurassic World, it
seems McFarr found his niche as Chris Pratt's

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.599
stunt double—he went on to double for Pratt
in 2016's Passengers and again the following

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.600
year in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2—a
role he prepared for by...playing with toy

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:37.460
guns?

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.230
"Ahhh!"

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.430
Nice.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.720
Bobby Holland Hanton—Thor

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.330
Bobby Holland Hanton is one of the most in-demand
stuntmen in Hollywood.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:55.140
He's doubled for Chris Evans' Captain America,
Christian Bale in The Dark Knight Rises, and

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:58.330
Ryan Reynolds in The Green Lantern, to name
a few.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:03.390
But if there's one gig he's especially proud
of, it's getting to bring the thunder as Thor

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:04.989
across the MCU.

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:10.370
From the costumes to the kick-ass stunt work,
Hanton loves everything about this gig, especially

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:15.780
star Chris Hemsworth, whom he described to
Business Insider as a legend, saying:

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.850
"Chris is in the best shape of any actor I've
seen.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.270
He's got huge arms and great coordination.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:26.410
I've never had to train so much in all my
life — three hours each session, twice a

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.970
day, six days a week.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:31.449
If Chris wasn't an actor, he'd be one of the
top stuntmen around."

00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:36.830
But even after all the high-wire stunts he's
performed in an Asgardian breastplate, Hanton's

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.120
favorite stunt is the prison scene in The
Dark Knight Rises.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:41.120
He said:

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.120
"I had to climb out of the prison he's in
and jump, miss the landing, fall 100 feet,

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.870
and slam into the opposite wall.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:53.050
It was one of my first ever high-falls, a
100-footer, which is quite a nice feat to

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.870
achieve for a stunt performer."

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.090
Sam Hargrave—Captain America

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:02.190
Although Bobby Holland Hanton has done some
stunts as Captain America, it's Sam Hargrave

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.500
who takes the brunt of the star-spangled beatings.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.310
When he isn't acting as the man behind Cap's
mask, he's also serving as Marvel's resident

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:15.400
stunt coordinator and choreographer, designing
some of the most memorable blowouts from Captain

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.810
America: The Winter Solider and Captain America:
Civil War.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:24.350
Chances are if one of Marvel's superheroes
takes a knuckle to the face, Hargrave is responsible

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.820
for it on some level.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.720
Clay Fontenot—Iron Man

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.570
We've come a long way from the chest shavings
and paint-on latex Robert Downey Jr. had to

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:34.360
endure for the first Iron Man.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:45.400
Between CGI and stuntmen, Robert Downey Jr.
barely ever has a reason to put on the Iron

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:50.710
Man suit anymore, which leaves Clay Fontenot
as the only guy who still has to suit up when

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.270
the cameras are rolling.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:57.220
Fontenot doubled for Downey Jr. in Iron Man,
Iron Man 2, and The Avengers, and he's done

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:02.181
stunt work on nearly 80 other films as well,
including Django Unchained, Guardians of the

00:06:02.181 --> 00:06:04.740
Galaxy, and all three Blade movies.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:08.930
Fontenot is easily one of the most prolific
stuntmen in the business.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:09.930
Thanks for watching!

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.449
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:12.449 --> 00:06:15.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

